      "body": "@abhishekacharya200 no changes needed from my side. Nothing in the processor needs the unlimited setting, and vLLM's port of the same model (`vllm/model_executor/models/nano_nemotron_vl.py`) never sets it either.\n\nThe new test fails when the line comes back, so it covers the change:\n\n```\n$ PYTHONPATH=python python -m pytest -q test/registered/unit/multimodal/test_nano_nemotron_vl_processor.py\n1 passed, 3 warnings in 11.46s          # head 6353660\n# with `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = None` restored in __init__:\nAssertionError: None != 89478485\n1 failed, 3 warnings in 11.35s\n```\n\nnon-blocking: once the guard is back, a NanoNemotron request with an image over 178,956,970 pixels gets a 500, not a 400. `DecompressionBombError` subclasses `Exception`, not `OSError`, so `_load_single_item` wraps it in `RuntimeError`. On main `279f1fa`, with every other model:\n\n```\n$ PYTHONPATH=python python bomb.py   # 15000 x 15000 1-bit PNG, 27385 bytes\nRuntimeError <- DecompressionBombError: ... Image size (225000000 pixels) exceeds limit of 178956970 pixels, could be decompression bomb DOS attack.\n```\n\nThat predates this PR and doesn't block it. The fix is one more entry in `CLIENT_MEDIA_EXCEPTIONS`, and it belongs in a separate PR so this one stays a single-line revert.\n",
